    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_39b5f8c0b288b3e81a6f506c03ec94a74f4663233a7765de93776d5ddd9e2d78",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Finite-height RH verification is a layered proof obligation: compute zeta with certified precision, turn critical-line values into localized roots, and compare the resulting critical-zero list with an independent count of all strip zeros. Euler-Maclaurin and Riemann-Siegel address certified evaluation, Hardy Z and Gram intervals address localization, Backlund and Turing address completeness, and Odlyzko-Schoenhage amortizes the evaluation layer for large batches.",
