    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5b33fa51b336277b2db5400e0de92ed59ccea1350ee773d7d3dd15dc8d13aeba",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Density-normalized pair correlation and the random-matrix dictionary turn zero data into precise predictions about repulsion, simplicity, and zeta moments that can be tested at very high zeros. The same sections keep the epistemic hierarchy explicit: smoothed conditional theorems and rigorous critical-line proportions are proofs within their hypotheses, whereas the unsmoothed correlation law, universal random-matrix transfer, and finite numerical agreement remain conjectural evidence.",
