    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_bc3ce7f568fdf7f0be7899195d87a643eb151c5572e58a1e4f6cf54bb30a5e9c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source presents a two-way analytic interface: Euler products and logarithmic differentiation encode prime and prime-power structure in zeta, while explicit formulas return zero information to weighted or unweighted prime counts. Across that interface, horizontal zero location controls attainable error exponents, and certified zero data through a finite height can support exact counts or explicit bounds over a correspondingly bounded arithmetic range.",
